952 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (addresses the two biggest sources of mis-spec returns: wrong configuration and wrong delivery expectations. Visual confidence at the decision point, before the buyer commits to a quote, cuts the order errors that show up months later in NPS and warranty data. Only 2 of 100 audited manufacturers disclose lead time, which is the size of the gap and the size of the opening for the next two or three to claim the position.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
953 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (The form is generating leads. Most of them are info- seekers, not buyers. The 15 manufacturers showing prices generate fewer leads, but each lead arrives with budget acknowledged and alternatives narrowed. Website pipeline that dealers will actually work is downstream of giving the buyer enough information to opt in.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
954 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (Pre-qualified leads close faster. A buyer who arrives with the product configured, intent expressed, and price acknowledged shortens the rep's discovery cycle. The site's job is discovery; the rep's job is the close. The cohort's median primary CTA is "Learn More," which converts curiosity into a click but not a click into a quote. Reducing friction at the quote stage is the cheapest single move in this audit. 12 of 100 already do it with low-friction inline forms of 8 fields or fewer, and those manufacturers cluster in the top quartile of Buyer Enablement Score.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
