3081 0 obj
<<
/Title (We selected 100 of the largest and most recognizable configurable-product manufacturing companies in North America, intentionally weighted toward companies with non-trivial channel structures \(dealers, distributors, reps\) and configurable physical products. The cohort was identified through a combination of public revenue rankings, trade-association member lists, and category coverage across the verticals where configurable selling is most material. The cohort is heterogeneous across company size, public/private status, and family ownership. It is not a probability sample of all configurable-product manufacturers; findings generalize to the cohort, not to the universe.)
